  "source_text": "Title: Aloo Paratha | Paratha Recipes | Potato Stuffed Paratha | Lunch Box Recipes | Dinner Recipes\n\nChannel: HomeCookingShow\n\nVideo description:\n\n📌 Perfect North Indian lunch ideas 🍛 👉 https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLFhw-Rie62rTkmGeKxQJlE5j9Zev8AbUq\n📌 Quick & tasty dinner ideas 🍽️ 👉 https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLFhw-Rie62rQg-5CF_EVldopnl7wyzC1Q\n📌 Easy & tasty stuffed veg parathas 👉https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLFhw-Rie62rScddPIoGUb9gQ2W2Zdowp0\n📌 Easy & tasty potato dishes 👉 https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLFhw-Rie62rSEXcnvN5E-CnK-HN0nboX4\n\nAloo Paratha | Paratha Recipes | Potato Stuffed Paratha | Lunch Box Recipes | Dinner Recipes\n\n\n\nAloo Paratha is a popular Indian flatbread made with a flavourful potato stuffing and cooked until soft and golden.\nThis homemade paratha recipe is perfect for lunch boxes, family lunches, or comforting dinners.\n\nIf you are looking for an easy aloo paratha, potato stuffed paratha, or a simple Indian paratha recipe,  or other paratha , this playlist  is  perfect for you, beginner‑friendly and easy to follow. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=58VEgUs_U1o&list=PLFhw-Rie62rQX_JuBd-9t7Xm2YKynGvyH&pp=sAgC\n\n\n\n\n#alooparatha #paratha #paratharecipe\n\nPrep time: 45 mins \nCook time: 45 mins \nNumber of servings: 4-5 persons \n\nIngredients\n\nWheat flour - 2 cup\nAjwain - 1/2 tsp\nPotatoes - 4 nos\nGreen chilies - 2 nos (chopped)\nGaram masala - 1/2 tsp\nKashmiri Red Chili Powder - 1 tsp\nChaat Masala Powder - 1/2 tsp\nCoriander leaves (chopped)\nWater\nOil \nSalt \n\nMethod \n\nMix wheat flour, carom seeds, salt and water and knead it to get a dough\nRest the dough while we make the filling \nBoil the potatoes and peel them and mash them roughly \nAdd green chilies, coriander leaves, red chili powder, garam masala powder, and chaat masala \nMix till everything is well combined\nDivide the dough into equal sized dough balls\nFlatten the dough balls and place the filling in the centre\nFold the flattened dough with the filling into a parcel\nFlatten it again and roll it out\nRoll out all the dough balls in the  same way\nHeat a tawa, place the rolled out parathas onto the hot tawa\nFlip the paratha once it is cooked on one side\nAdd some oil on the edges and cook on both sides till they turn golden\nServe the Aloo Paratha hot.Aloo Paratha\n\nYou can buy our book and classes on http://www.21frames.in/shop\n\nHAPPY COOKING WITH HOMECOOKING\nENJOY OUR RECIPES\n\nWEBSITE: http://www.21frames.in/homecooking\nFACEBOOK - https://www.facebook.com/HomeCookingShow\nYOUTUBE: https://www.youtube.com/user/VentunoHomeCooking \nINSTAGRAM - https://www.instagram.com/homecookingshow\nA Ventuno Production: http://www.ventunotech.com",
